 ## 2026-08-19

+### 0400 — Provider graph validation follows target-owned PBX build phases (BUG-260819-8qf0s0)
+- REVIEW REWORK: Global `project.pbxproj` substring checks were false-green when the provider's adapter Frameworks edge or relay Resources edge was removed while product/file declarations remained. The validator now resolves the unique `ReluxProxyMacTunnel` `PBXNativeTarget`, follows its referenced `PBXFrameworksBuildPhase` and `PBXResourcesBuildPhase`, and dereferences the exact build-file product/file edges.
+- REGRESSION: Generated-project adversarial fixtures remove each target-owned edge independently while preserving global declarations; both are required to exit nonzero. Existing source graph, relay manifest/checksum, no-dlopen, and evidence-only `CReluxNativeFixture` negatives remain enforced.
+- VERIFICATION: The focused negative suite, full credential-free matrix, Python/shell syntax checks, strict Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. No signing, installation, launch, VPN preference/tunnel, route, or DNS operation was performed.
+
 ### 0430 — Clean generated-project matrix is false-green on the accepted provider graph (TASK-260715-nphtib)
 - VERIFICATION: A detached no-hardlink clone of revision `409b3b4151c9f2f7bac7392595583b3fe971e455` passed the repository-owned credential-free matrix in 316.05 seconds: deterministic double generation, the exact six macOS-only schemes and four Xcode targets, unsigned Debug/Release host/provider builds, 443 Swift tests in 37 suites, native packaging, relay artifact validation, and pinned legacy v0.1.0 tests/build. Strict Swift format lint also passed; coverage reported 93.30% lines, 91.44% functions, and 85.67% regions.
 - REGRESSION: The green gate does not enforce the accepted ADR section 3.1 provider dependency/resource row. `Project.swift` generates `ReluxProxyMacTunnel -> ReluxTunnelCore` only; it does not add `ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter` or a verified relay resource, and the Release provider contains neither adapter/native symbols nor a relay payload. The earlier target log records this as intentionally deferred because of the SwiftPM/Xcode binary-output collision, but the verification task has no accepted ADR exception and therefore cannot claim an exact-graph pass.
