 - PRIVACY PROCESS: An initial prerequisite check used an unnecessarily broad parent-directory listing, which exposed unrelated local filenames in the automated spawn log. Accepted evidence must use task-scoped existence/version probes only. The persisted spawn log is sanitized before review and the task outcome contains no unrelated local filename or path.

+### 0400 — Provider graph validation follows target-owned PBX build phases (BUG-260819-8qf0s0)
+- REVIEW REWORK: Global `project.pbxproj` substring checks were false-green when the provider's adapter Frameworks edge or relay Resources edge was removed while product/file declarations remained. The validator now resolves the unique `ReluxProxyMacTunnel` `PBXNativeTarget`, follows its referenced `PBXFrameworksBuildPhase` and `PBXResourcesBuildPhase`, and dereferences the exact build-file product/file edges.
+- REGRESSION: Generated-project adversarial fixtures remove each target-owned edge independently while preserving global declarations; both are required to exit nonzero. Existing source graph, relay manifest/checksum, no-dlopen, and evidence-only `CReluxNativeFixture` negatives remain enforced.
+- VERIFICATION: The focused negative suite, full credential-free matrix, Python/shell syntax checks, strict Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. No signing, installation, launch, VPN preference/tunnel, route, or DNS operation was performed.
+
 ### 0148 — Credential-free generated-project gate closes exact-graph and clean-runner gaps (TASK-260715-sbrrp7)
 - REVIEW REWORK: Workspace scheme validation now compares the complete normalized six-scheme set. Regression fixtures reject missing-only, unexpected-only, and the prior substring-alias case where `ReluxProxyMacTunnel` masked a missing `ReluxProxyMac`.
 - CI BOOTSTRAP: The macOS pull-request lane installs Mise 2026.3.10 through `jdx/mise-action` pinned to commit `3c2e0cf82a5b2e5249f0d3635a4d83d0ae861518` and verifies the macOS arm64 binary SHA-256 matching the arm64 `macos-15` runner before invoking the repository-owned Make entry point. A contract regression keeps the runner label and checksum paired. Tuist installation remains pinned and owned by that entry point.
